Tom, thanks for the diagram. Copying your work address so this lands in the right place, and Dana, who'll own the technical side of any pilot.

1. Outbound: the agent needs one outbound HTTPS connection to our control plane (a single hostname, port 443). It works fine through an authenticated proxy. Order and labor data stay on the agent; only aggregate metrics leave the building.
2. Fulcrum: we subscribe to the event stream rather than polling, so steady-state load is under 5 requests/second. The initial backfill is throttled to 10/second and runs overnight.

Dana can walk your network team through it whenever suits.

Jack

